  "limitations": [
    "Identity snapshots detect replacement; they are not content hashes, plan authentication, locked trees or atomic ancestor containment.",
    "In-place changes, inode/device reuse and unusual remote filesystem identities remain boundaries; same-device bind mounts require separate qualification.",
    "Windows lint cross-compilation is not Windows runtime, NTFS/ReFS/SMB, junction, Bun/native parity or installer proof; macOS/ARM64 runtime remains open.",
    "A failed recursive deletion may already have removed descendants; SIGKILL or power loss cannot flush a terminal report.",
    "100 warm local samples provide empirical percentiles, not cold/network storage or production tail guarantees; host terminal painting is excluded.",
    "Sampled RSS and logical budgets do not prove absence of leaks or immunity to OOM; the 200 GiB fixture was sparse metadata, not allocated data deletion.",
    "Competing applies, trash destination races, crash-durable recovery, dependency advisory/license provenance and actual installed packages remain release work.",
    "Rust wide-stream host event-loop p99 was about 13 ms; parsing/planning and full terminal interaction still require profiling."
  ],
  "logsNote": "Ephemeral /tmp logs supplement durable benchmark JSON and regression tests; this is local evidence, not hosted CI or release evidence."
